  "body": "Direct-PR: three citations in docs, restored on the operator's request\n\n**Problem.** #586 cited the local AQ server as `toyo@96c0aea`, without its owner, so the AGPL source it ran cannot be found from the docs.\n\n**Cause.** I took the owner's GitHub ID out of the citation, thinking it had to stay out. The operator ruled on 2026-11-07 that the GitHub ID may be cited.\n\n**Change.** `toyo@96c0aea` becomes `roger21/toyo@96c0aea` in `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` (2) and the corpus `MANIFEST.md` (1). Nothing else; the metas keep `toyo/aq`, which the kit closes as a fixed value. The body of #574 is restored to its original text too.\n\n**Tests.** `check --corpus` 549 of 549 clean, `pre-commit run --all-files` passes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified the documented responses for local-instance report submissions: `1` indicates a new AQ or message was added, while `-2`, `-3`, and `-4` indicate an unknown AQ ID, an empty new-AQ name, and a duplicate report, respectively.\n  * Documented that requests with a `post_url` not starting with `https://forum.hardware.fr` receive a 403 response with an empty body.\n  * Updated the cited source reference for the Run 13 captures.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
